              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If you are asked to identify and describe the instrument, say:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is a Deaver retractor. It is a handheld, non-self-retaining surgical retractor made commonly of stainless steel. It consists of a handle, shaft and broad, deeply curved blade. It is used for deep retraction, particularly during open abdominal surgery, to improve exposure of underlying structures. Its advantages include good reach and a broad contact surface. Its limitations include the need for an assistant and the risk of pressure-related tissue injury if excessive force is applied.”",
                  "style": "quote"
                }
              ]
